---
import fs from 'node:fs';
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import SourceBlock from '../components/SourceBlock.astro';
import { getRegistry } from '../lib/harness/registry.ts';
import { compatibility, vendorFile } from '../lib/harness/paths.ts';

const r = getRegistry();
const config = fs.readFileSync(vendorFile('config.example.json'), 'utf8').trim();
const planned = compatibility().clients
  .filter((client: { id: string; status: string }) => client.status === 'planned')
  .map((client: { id: string }) => client.id);

const clone = [
  'git clone https://github.com/JakeSelby/model-citizen.git ~/repos/agent-harness',
  'cd ~/repos/agent-harness',
  'bin/citizen install',
  '# Homebrew packages, VS Code + extensions, Claude Code, Codex, gh, then sync',
].join('\n');
const adopt = 'bin/citizen sync --dry-run\nbin/citizen sync';
const after = ['bin/citizen doctor    # versions, logins, links, drift', 'bin/citizen diff      # what changed since the last sync', 'bin/citizen uninstall # put everything back'].join('\n');

const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'install', text: 'Install' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'existing', text: 'Link an existing setup' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'configure', text: 'Configure' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'check', text: 'Check and undo' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Install and configure"
  description="Clone the harness, run one command, edit one JSON file. Choose runtime targets, inspect your stance selections, and review configuration ownership before syncing."
  crumbs={[{ label: 'install' }]}
  sourcePath="README.md"
  sourceLabel="View README on GitHub"
  headings={headings}
  kind="Page"
>
  <div class="eyebrow"><span class="pill amber">Start here</span></div>
  <h1>Install and configure</h1>
  <p class="lede">Clone, run one command, edit one JSON file. An agent can do all of it from the README; inspect support and configuration ownership before syncing.</p>

  <p>
    Claude Code and Codex are integration targets. Check the <a href="/compatibility/">versioned compatibility catalog</a>
    {planned.length > 0 && <span>; planned in it: {planned.join(', ')}</span>}.
  </p>
  <div class="harness-prose">
    <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
    <p>On a fresh machine, <code>install</code> brings in the tools and then links the harness in:</p>
    <SourceBlock code={clone} lang="sh" label="Fresh machine" />

    <h2 id="existing">Link an existing setup</h2>
    <p>If Claude Code, Codex and VS Code are already installed, skip straight to the sync. Unmanaged files require explicit adoption; modified owned files produce conflicts and are preserved.</p>
    <SourceBlock code={adopt} lang="sh" label="Tools already installed" />

    <h2 id="configure">Configure</h2>
    <p>
      Copy <code>config.example.json</code> to <code>~/.config/agent-harness/config.json</code>, put your name and stances in it, and run <code>bin/citizen sync</code> again.
      Keep personal identity outside the checkout. Each stance key selects one policy projected into the runtimes you enable.
    </p>
    <SourceBlock code={config} lang="json" label="config.example.json" />
    <p>Each key under <code>stances</code> is a dimension; the value names the variant that loads on every turn.</p>
    <ul>
      {r.stances.map((d) => (
        <li>
          <a href={d.route}><code>{d.id}</code></a>: {d.variants.map((v) => v.variant).join(' · ')}
          {d.defaultVariant && <span class="muted small"> — default <code>{d.defaultVariant}</code></span>}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p>Session stance choices are explicit and scoped; they never grant native permissions. Inspect effective selections with <code>citizen stances --json</code>.</p>

    <h2 id="check">Check and undo</h2>
    <SourceBlock code={after} lang="sh" label="After the sync" />
    <p>In a session, <code>/context</code> lists the harness rules and the selected stances; <code>/hooks</code> lists the hooks. The <a href="/docs/sync-model/">sync model</a> and <a href="/docs/settings-ownership/">settings ownership</a> pages say exactly what the sync touches and what it never will.</p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
